WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:03.240
- [Narrator] Amami Ōshima is an island

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.840
off the coast of mainland Japan.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:06.930
And while it's well-known

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:10.200
for its thriving coral
reefs and sandy beaches,

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.443
it's sumo that puts
this island on the map.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:20.640
Amami Ōshima takes great
pride in raising young boys

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.063
to become some of the
country's best wrestlers.

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:30.456
- [Jiro] (speaking in foreign language)

00:00:49.964 --> 00:00:54.060
- [Narrator] With over
150 dohyōs, or sumo rings,

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.250
Amami Ōshima has the highest concentration

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.490
of sumo facilities in Japan,

00:00:58.490 --> 00:00:59.930
making the sport accessible

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:01.703
to most young people on the island.

00:01:04.914 --> 00:01:08.997
- (speaking in foreign language)

00:01:21.151 --> 00:01:25.818
- [Jiro] (speaking in foreign language)

00:01:30.943 --> 00:01:32.760
- [Narrator] But sumo
is not only practiced

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:34.810
as a means for future success;

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:37.150
it's a nod to the island's history

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:40.100
and has been embedded in its
culture for hundreds of years.

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:48.160
Annual festivals include sumo tournaments

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:50.363
where wrestlers come out to participate.

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:56.501
- [Jiro] (speaking in foreign language)

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:09.260
- [Narrator] But despite
the island's efforts

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:12.210
to maintain sumo as a cultural staple,

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:14.500
the sport has begun to
decrease in popularity

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.231
among young people.

00:02:16.231 --> 00:02:20.314
- (speaking in foreign language)

